WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.453 --> 00:00:09.827
so why did a surprise guest come to chit-chat?&nbsp;
And who's the real hero in this movie?

00:00:10.273 --> 00:00:14.833
If you saw the 2019 film "Shazam" then&nbsp;
you may recall the scene in which Billy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:19.813
Batson is first transported to the Rock&nbsp;
of Eternity to meet the wizard Shazam.

00:00:19.813 --> 00:00:24.353
"My name is Shazam."

00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:28.263
"Wait, for real?"

00:00:28.263 --> 00:00:32.893
As Billy tries to make sense of what's going&nbsp;
on, Shazam explains that he is the last of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.893 --> 00:00:36.853
council of wizards and he is looking for&nbsp;
someone pure of heart to pass his powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:41.833
onto in order to protect humanity from the&nbsp;
seven deadly sins. The reason he has to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:46.693
so picky is because the last time the power&nbsp;
was passed to someone ... it didn't go so well.

00:00:46.693 --> 00:00:51.313
We learn a bit more about that in this&nbsp;
film, because Black Adam, or Teth-Adam as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.313 --> 00:00:55.513
he's originally called, is the reason Shazam&nbsp;
has to be careful about who gets the powers.

00:00:55.513 --> 00:01:00.553
Bestowed with the stamina of Shu, the&nbsp;
speed of Horus, the strength of Amon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.553 --> 00:01:07.033
the wisdom of Zehuti, the Powers of Aten and the&nbsp;
courage of Mehen, Adam used his incredible powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:12.553
to seek revenge on the ruler of Kahndaq instead&nbsp;
of being the hero the seven wizards intended.

00:01:12.553 --> 00:01:17.473
The story of "Black Adam" is about the character&nbsp;
gradually getting to a place mentally where he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.473 --> 00:01:22.213
embody some of the attributes the wizards were&nbsp;
looking for. However, since he was not the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:26.579
they initially chose to wield the power,&nbsp;
he will never become a traditional hero.

00:01:27.274 --> 00:01:33.733
5,000 years after Teth Adam brought down Anh-Kot,&nbsp;
a woman named Adrianna Tomaz releases him from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:38.653
prison by speaking the words engraved on the&nbsp;
seal trapping him in some kind of limbo state.

00:01:38.653 --> 00:01:43.513
The second he shows up, Adam goes on a&nbsp;
lightning-spitting rampage as he kills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.513 --> 00:01:47.773
the soldiers coming at him with guns and&nbsp;
tanks, and all sorts of useless weapons.

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:51.733
Since the legends say that Teth Adam&nbsp;
would return when Kahndaq needs him most,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:55.333
everyone naturally assumes that this&nbsp;
super-strong guy who looks like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:59.593
statue they built thousands of years ago&nbsp;
is there to rescue them from Intergang.

00:01:59.593 --> 00:02:04.273
Unfortunately, they couldn't be more wrong. The&nbsp;
only reason Adam has killed those men is because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.273 --> 00:02:08.473
they were in his way and they were attacking&nbsp;
him — he has no intention of saving anyone.

00:02:08.473 --> 00:02:12.493
This doesn't fit with all the legends they've&nbsp;
heard, and there's a good reason for that:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.493 --> 00:02:17.533
this isn't the Teth-Adam the wizards initially&nbsp;
chose to have their powers. They selected the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:21.253
boy Hurut, who was the son of the man&nbsp;
currently carrying the name Teth-Adam.

00:02:21.253 --> 00:02:26.113
Hurut gave his powers to his father to&nbsp;
protect him, but was assassinated shortly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.113 --> 00:02:30.733
after. Therefore, the man flying around&nbsp;
modern-day Kahndaq is a broken father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.733 --> 00:02:35.685
who's lost the only thing he's ever loved,&nbsp;
and who sees his own existence as a curse.

00:02:35.932 --> 00:02:40.453
The Justice Society of America is called&nbsp;
in to take Adam into custody because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.453 --> 00:02:44.533
poses a threat to the safety of the&nbsp;
United States and every other country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.533 --> 00:02:47.893
in the world if he were to suddenly&nbsp;
decide he'd like to rule the world.

00:02:47.893 --> 00:02:52.273
Black Adam's rage and thirst for vengeance&nbsp;
released the seven deadly sins upon the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.273 --> 00:02:54.493
resulting in six of the seven wizards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.493 --> 00:02:58.453
getting obliterated and entire&nbsp;
civilizations being wiped out.

00:02:58.453 --> 00:03:02.653
Despite being the "good guys," the&nbsp;
Justice Society has inherited Amanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.653 --> 00:03:07.093
Waller's sanctimonious attitude when it&nbsp;
comes to what heroes can and cannot do.

00:03:07.093 --> 00:03:11.053
Aside from continuously lecturing&nbsp;
Adam on proper heroic etiquette,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.053 --> 00:03:15.733
they also just assume that the people of&nbsp;
Kahndaq are going to step aside for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.733 --> 00:03:21.254
Justice Society. Why? Because they're the ones&nbsp;
with the superpowers, therefore they know best.

00:03:21.254 --> 00:03:24.719
"You think yourself a hero but you&nbsp;
would let these criminals go free."

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:27.250
"Heroes don’t kill people."

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:32.113
However, this is a country that has been invaded&nbsp;
and occupied for years, and not once did the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.113 --> 00:03:37.693
Justice Society come to help. Only after the JSA&nbsp;
can learn to work with Adam and the citizens of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.693 --> 00:03:43.213
Kahndaq are they able to get any work done. We see&nbsp;
that at the end, when instead of charging in and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.213 --> 00:03:49.115
destroying things, Atom Smasher and Cyclone use&nbsp;
their powers to work in tandem with the people.

00:03:49.393 --> 00:03:53.953
When "Black Adam" opens, we're given a very&nbsp;
detailed breakdown of everything that went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.953 --> 00:04:00.673
down in Kahndaq in the year 2600 BC, thanks&nbsp;
to a voiceover from the character Amon Tomaz.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:05.293
He tells us all about how a magical element&nbsp;
called Eternium can be found in Kahndaq,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.293 --> 00:04:10.513
and that an ancient ruler had his slaves dig for&nbsp;
the element in order to forge the Crown of Sabbac&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.513 --> 00:04:15.613
so he could wield ultimate power. However, Black&nbsp;
Adam took the crown and destroyed his empire.

00:04:15.613 --> 00:04:19.693
In this prologue, we see Hurut with an&nbsp;
old man, but once we get the full story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.693 --> 00:04:25.393
we realize that the old man was actually the boy's&nbsp;
father, and he looks remarkably like Black Adam.

00:04:25.393 --> 00:04:30.493
While a tad confusing at first, this actually&nbsp;
demonstrates just how much of Kahndaq's past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.493 --> 00:04:34.933
and resources had been co-opted by&nbsp;
outside forces over the centuries.

00:04:34.933 --> 00:04:39.973
When the Justice Society explains they've had&nbsp;
access to ancient texts that say Black Adam was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.973 --> 00:04:43.753
a destroyer instead of a hero, Amon's&nbsp;
mother Adrianna doesn't believe them.

00:04:43.753 --> 00:04:47.653
It is very likely that people have been&nbsp;
coming to Kahndaq and stealing from it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:50.593
so much, that even its own history is incomplete.

00:04:50.593 --> 00:04:55.033
Therefore, when we see Amon's story, what&nbsp;
we're seeing is his interpretation of events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:59.653
not the events as they actually unfolded.&nbsp;
This stands as yet another reason why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.653 --> 00:05:03.160
Kahndaq needs a protector:&nbsp;
to keep their history intact.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.780
"I kneel before no one."

00:05:05.353 --> 00:05:08.353
When the truth comes out that Black&nbsp;
Adam isn't the hero of legend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.353 --> 00:05:13.393
he agrees to go with the JSA to be locked up&nbsp;
forever. He doesn't want these powers anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.393 --> 00:05:15.913
since he never felt worthy of them to begin with.

00:05:15.913 --> 00:05:21.253
He makes the JSA promise that after he says&nbsp;
"Shazam" and transforms back to his original form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:25.573
they will never allow him to speak the&nbsp;
word again. He is tired of carrying this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.573 --> 00:05:30.013
burden and welcomes the idea of being free&nbsp;
of it, even if that means being locked up.

00:05:30.013 --> 00:05:35.113
They take him to an underwater Task Force X&nbsp;
prison run by Amanda Waller. She, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.113 --> 00:05:40.633
is the director of A.R.G.U.S, an agency that&nbsp;
engages in numerous clandestine missions across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.633 --> 00:05:44.773
the globe to make sure superhumans do not&nbsp;
threaten the security of the United States.

00:05:44.773 --> 00:05:49.513
Task Force X is a division of A.R.G.U.S.&nbsp;
where imprisoned villains in the DC Universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.513 --> 00:05:53.233
are used to carry out many of those&nbsp;
missions in exchange for time off of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.233 --> 00:05:56.713
their sentences. You might remember&nbsp;
them better as The Suicide Squad.

00:05:56.713 --> 00:06:01.153
"Well, we consider that term degrading.&nbsp;
The official term is Task Force X."

00:06:01.153 --> 00:06:05.293
When the members of the JSA arrive,&nbsp;
they're greeted by Emilia Harcourt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.293 --> 00:06:10.093
Fans of the HBO series "Peacemaker"&nbsp;
will likely remember her as an NSA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.093 --> 00:06:14.473
agent working for Waller in that series&nbsp;
and in the film "The Suicide Squad."

00:06:14.473 --> 00:06:19.153
She points out that the Gods were meant to be&nbsp;
humanity's heroes, but humanity seems to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.153 --> 00:06:24.554
one always burying them. All of this suggests that&nbsp;
Task Force X is powerful enough to control Adam.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:28.330
"Funny for you how often the only&nbsp;
choice in killing people coincides."

00:06:28.813 --> 00:06:33.193
Doctor Fate is a man with a thousand storm&nbsp;
clouds swirling over his head at all times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.193 --> 00:06:38.413
as the sentient Alien Helmet of Nabu he wears&nbsp;
reveals every possible version of the future.

00:06:38.413 --> 00:06:43.153
He knows that the future is unwritten, but&nbsp;
due to circumstances out of his control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.153 --> 00:06:47.533
he can't always predict which series of&nbsp;
events will unfold. His job is to step&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.533 --> 00:06:52.393
in and make sure that the decisions made by&nbsp;
the JSA result in the best possible outcome.

00:06:52.393 --> 00:06:56.233
Throughout much of the film, he is dreading&nbsp;
the completion of the mission because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.233 --> 00:07:00.777
knows the version of events where they save&nbsp;
the day requires his friend Hawkman to die.

00:07:00.777 --> 00:07:02.217
"Nothing but heartache."

00:07:02.217 --> 00:07:06.253
When Sabbac rises from the underworld&nbsp;
to conquer Earth, Fate knows the "happy"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.253 --> 00:07:12.313
ending is approaching, but he's not about to let&nbsp;
Hawkman go. He steps in and sacrifices himself.

00:07:12.313 --> 00:07:16.813
While doing so, he uses his power to&nbsp;
be in two places at once to free Adam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.813 --> 00:07:20.953
because he knows Adam is the only&nbsp;
one powerful enough to defeat Sabbac.

00:07:20.953 --> 00:07:25.993
He tells Adam that he should accept his abilities&nbsp;
because "Fate doesn't make mistakes," and at that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.993 --> 00:07:31.213
moment Doctor Fate has literally chosen Adam&nbsp;
to save humanity — whether he wants it or not.

00:07:31.213 --> 00:07:34.993
Fate's sacrifice also allows&nbsp;
Hawkman to hold the helmet in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.993 --> 00:07:39.974
order to multiply himself and distract&nbsp;
Sabbac, turning the tide of the battle.

00:07:40.333 --> 00:07:43.513
Despite his many faults, the&nbsp;
antagonist of the film isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.513 --> 00:07:46.273
actually Black Adam. It’s a man named Ishmael.

00:07:46.273 --> 00:07:51.613
At first, he appears to be working with Adrianna&nbsp;
to help free Kahndaq, but he's actually looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.613 --> 00:07:56.293
for the Crown of Sabbac. No one really knows&nbsp;
why he wants it, so they check the engraving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.293 --> 00:08:01.453
within it, only to find that it reads that life&nbsp;
is the only road to death, which seems obvious.

00:08:01.453 --> 00:08:05.113
What they don't know is that the power&nbsp;
from the crown comes from the underworld,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.113 --> 00:08:07.633
which serves as a dark reflection of our world.

00:08:07.633 --> 00:08:11.953
This means the inscription is really telling&nbsp;
them that death is the only road to life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.953 --> 00:08:15.553
Ishmael wants the crown because he&nbsp;
is the descendent of King Anh-Kot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.553 --> 00:08:18.913
and only his bloodline can wear&nbsp;
the crown and use its power.

00:08:18.913 --> 00:08:22.513
When Ishmael gets the crown, he is&nbsp;
killed and sent to the underworld,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.513 --> 00:08:26.533
where six demons grant him the&nbsp;
evil version of Black Adam's power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.533 --> 00:08:30.493
and he rises from that realm to command&nbsp;
an undead army to conquer the world.

00:08:30.493 --> 00:08:35.053
Black Adam is the only one who can stop&nbsp;
him. After briefly visiting the afterlife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.053 --> 00:08:40.273
where his son tells him it isn't his time yet,&nbsp;
Adam returns to Kahndaq and battles Sabbac.

00:08:40.273 --> 00:08:46.273
While he handles that, ordinary citizens fight his&nbsp;
skeleton army. Finally, Adam rips Sabbac in half,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.273 --> 00:08:51.721
destroying the crown and Sabbac's power,&nbsp;
at last freeing Kahndaq — for now, that is.

00:08:51.721 --> 00:08:53.264
"We’ll take care of the rest."

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:57.793
As the dust begins to settle and everyone&nbsp;
realizes the battle has been won,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.793 --> 00:09:02.113
the question posed to Adam is whether or&nbsp;
not he is willing to be Kahndaq's hero.

00:09:02.113 --> 00:09:06.373
He destroys the throne meant for their&nbsp;
savior because it feels wrong. Even after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.153 --> 00:09:11.593
5,000 years of imprisonment, Adam knows that&nbsp;
Kahndaq doesn't need a ruler — it needs people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.593 --> 00:09:14.533
who are willing to work together&nbsp;
to return it to its former glory.

00:09:14.533 --> 00:09:20.053
"Kahndaq already has heroes," he says, having met&nbsp;
people like Adrianna and her son Amon who believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.053 --> 00:09:25.453
in Kahndaq and want to see it thrive again. Their&nbsp;
hearts and intentions are pure, unlike his own.

00:09:25.453 --> 00:09:29.173
This goes back to the start of the&nbsp;
film, when Hurut stresses the need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.173 --> 00:09:33.373
for everyone to stand up and fight their&nbsp;
enslavers when everyone else is too scared.

00:09:33.373 --> 00:09:39.073
Adrianna and Amon are this generation's version of&nbsp;
Hurut. With Intergang gone and Sabbac killed, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.073 --> 00:09:44.593
can organize the citizens to work together. While&nbsp;
that's going on, Kahndaq still needs a protector,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.593 --> 00:09:49.753
someone who can stand in the way when an invading&nbsp;
force shows up looking to occupy them again.

00:09:49.753 --> 00:09:54.733
That is the role Adam is more comfortable with,&nbsp;
because he still isn't one for rescuing people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.733 --> 00:09:59.713
He will not save Kahndaq, but he will punish and&nbsp;
destroy anyone who thinks they can invade it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.713 --> 00:10:05.327
This is a sign that he is moving away from being&nbsp;
a total anti-hero and compromising a little bit.

00:10:05.653 --> 00:10:08.773
Adam is released from his prison and&nbsp;
enters a world already flush with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.773 --> 00:10:11.353
super-powered beings capable of incredible feats.

00:10:11.353 --> 00:10:16.513
By the end of the film, Adam has been reborn:&nbsp;
his suit is more vibrant, he's been encouraged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.513 --> 00:10:20.593
by the spirit of his son to do more, and&nbsp;
he even changes his name to Black Adam.

00:10:20.593 --> 00:10:23.833
Thus, he is more reminiscent of the&nbsp;
character we know from the comics:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.833 --> 00:10:28.333
a character capable of doing good, but&nbsp;
with dubious morals and the potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.333 --> 00:10:32.413
to go from good to evil depending&nbsp;
on the situation. This is, perhaps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.413 --> 00:10:36.727
why Amanda Waller isn't very happy about&nbsp;
him not remaining in her underwater prison.

00:10:37.033 --> 00:10:39.313
Once the end credit sequence comes to a close,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.313 --> 00:10:43.873
we fade up to see a drone descending from&nbsp;
the sky before Black Adam. A hologram of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.873 --> 00:10:48.313
Amanda Waller projects from the device&nbsp;
and she, as usual, doesn't look happy.

00:10:48.313 --> 00:10:52.993
She tells him that since he won't be staying in&nbsp;
her prison, he is required to remain in Kahndaq.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.993 --> 00:10:57.673
If he steps beyond its borders, she'll make&nbsp;
sure it's the last thing he ever does. Since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.673 --> 00:11:01.693
he isn't fond of serving a master, Adam&nbsp;
tells her no one on Earth can stop him.

00:11:01.693 --> 00:11:06.193
She threatens to "call in a favor" with&nbsp;
beings from other planets. He tells her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.193 --> 00:11:10.393
to send them all. The hologram ends and&nbsp;
we see Superman emerge from the shadows.

00:11:10.393 --> 00:11:14.713
He tells Adam that it's been a while since anyone&nbsp;
has frightened the people of Earth quite as much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.713 --> 00:11:19.453
as he has, suggesting that Black Adam's presence&nbsp;
is akin to the arrival of Superman himself.

00:11:19.453 --> 00:11:24.493
Although he says he just wants to talk, Black&nbsp;
Adam's penchant for foregoing discussion in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.493 --> 00:11:29.173
favor of violence pretty much guarantees&nbsp;
their conversation will not go well. Perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.173 --> 00:11:32.773
that means the sequel could feature a&nbsp;
fight between Black Adam and Superman.

00:11:32.773 --> 00:11:36.013
Hopefully, a potential "Black&nbsp;
Adam 2" can also explain why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.013 --> 00:11:38.593
Superman would do favors for someone like Waller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.593 --> 00:11:43.213
given her shady tactics. Perhaps she didn't&nbsp;
send him and he really did just come to talk.

